2. Abstract

Abstract:This white sheet introduces the Blackwell Identity‑Wave Telemetry Framework and its implementation within the SUPRAKERNEL_v1.0.1 Digital Blueprint Simulation System. Traditional telemetry measures physical state variables (pressure, temperature, speed, curvature) but fails to capture the persistent identity of phenomena across datasets, systems, and time. The Blackwell framework defines a new class of measurement—identity‑aware telemetry—by constructing an identity-wave (\Psi_{\text{identity}}) from heterogeneous astrophysical datasets and coupling it to a unified time‑perturbation field (\Delta t'(x,t)). A universal identity field (\Psi_{\text{universal}}) is introduced as the missing coherence substrate, and a Temporal Stability Extractor (TSE) operator is defined to quantify identity‑wave stability. Together, these components form a new architecture for simulation, sensing, and data fusion that extends beyond conventional physics and engineering paradigms.

